{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793655834,"nonce":"cX/ZYNtIbY6pl/nIo1ce65rTm5o=","title":"Establish shared Cloud Sync document histories and durable exchange","message":"Parent: cd54ac37bbbdfea0fa1fcd39288738a7c0b48475ed9ecea3e6cc98ad20c109ed.\n\nContinuous sync needs an authoritative common Yrs lineage. Independent native/session documents currently seed identical disk text as different edits; exchanging them directly duplicates it. Implement the first transport-independent milestone: deterministic seed from the published workspace/file generation; owner/capability-scoped open and exchange; durable bounded incremental journal with compaction, checksums, quota and no idle retained graphs; stale lineage/dependency refusal; and snapshot publication fencing so pending document edits are not discarded by whole-tree saves.\n\nTest independent replicas, concurrent/Unicode edits, deletions, duplicate/reordered delivery, offline catch-up, corrupted and incomplete updates, quota/storage refusal, gateway restart and snapshot changes/recreated paths. Include a real Rust client exercised against the local Rust Worker fixture. Existing session recovery and its credentials remain separate. Automatic editor binding and pushed update delivery follow this foundation; do not advertise continuous editor sync until those are wired and verified.","files":null}]}